{"tool_name":"cem","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cem","home":"http://alumni.cs.ucr.edu/~liw/cem.html","summary":"CEM is an algorithm to assemble transcripts and estimate their expression levels from RNA-Seq reads.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:04:37Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:35:08.612563Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["0.9.1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cem","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://alumni.cs.ucr.edu/~liw/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["Citation instructions"],"url":"http://alumni.cs.ucr.edu/~liw/cem.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Transcriptome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3258"}]}],"name":"CEM","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bts559","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: RNA-Seq uses the high-throughput sequencing technology to identify and quantify transcriptome at an unprecedented high resolution and low cost. However, RNA-Seq reads are usually not uniformly distributed and biases in RNA-Seq data post great challenges in many applications including transcriptome assembly and the expression level estimation of genes or isoforms. Much effort has been made in the literature to calibrate the expression level estimation from biased RNA-Seq data, but the effect of biases on transcriptome assembly remains largely unexplored.Results: Here, we propose a statistical framework for both transcriptome assembly and isoform expression level estimation from biased RNA-Seq data. Using a quasi-multinomial distribution model, our method is able to capture various types of RNA-Seq biases, including positional, sequencing and mappability biases. Our experimental results on simulated and real RNA-Seq datasets exhibit interesting effects of RNA-Seq biases on both transcriptome assembly and isoform expression level estimation. The advantage of our method is clearly shown in the experimental analysis by its high sensitivity and precision in transcriptome assembly and the high concordance of its estimated expression levels with quantitative reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction data. \u00a9 2012 The Author.","authors":[{"name":"Jiang T."},{"name":"Li W."}],"citationCount":62,"date":"2012-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Transcriptome assembly and isoform expression level estimation from biased RNA-Seq reads"},"pmcid":"PMC3496342","pmid":"23060617","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CEM","home":"https://bio.tools/cem","version":"0.9.1","summary":"CEM is an algorithm to assemble transcripts and estimate their expression levels from RNA-Seq reads.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:cem:0.9.1/cmd/alumni.cs.ucr.edu","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"citation":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":44,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":1,"year":"2025"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":4,"year":"2021"},{"count":5,"year":"2013"},{"count":5,"year":"2016"},{"count":6,"year":"2014"},{"count":6,"year":"2015"},{"count":6,"year":"2017"},{"count":6,"year":"2018"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bts559","pmcid":"PMC3496342","pmid":"23060617","ref_count":37,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":2,"year":"2006"},{"count":4,"year":"2008"},{"count":8,"year":"2009"},{"count":8,"year":"2011"},{"count":12,"year":"2010"}],"title":"Transcriptome assembly and isoform expression level estimation from biased RNA-Seq reads.","year":2012}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":false}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/cem","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>Computer-assisted Evaluation of Myelin formation (CEM) is a collection designed to automate myelin quantification. It requires use input to choose the best threshold values. The myelin is calculated as an overlap between neuronal signal and oligodendrocyte signal. Results are given as pixel counts and percents.</p>\n\n<p>CEM runs as an imageJ plugin with an optional Matlab extension to remove cell bodies. More details are published at <a href=\"http://dev.biologists.org/content/142/12/2213.long\">Kerman et al. 2015 <em>Development</em></a>. Supplemental Material includes a detailed <a href=\"http://dev.biologists.org/content/develop/suppl/2015/06/10/dev.116517.DC1/DEV116517supp.pdf\">user manual</a> and the <a href=\"http://bilalkermanlab.com/cem/\">download link</a>.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>Computer-assisted Evaluation of Myelin formation (CEM) is a collection designed to automate myelin quantification. It requires use input to choose the best threshold values. The myelin is calculated as an overlap between neuronal signal and oligodendrocyte signal. Results are given as pixel counts and percents.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>CEM runs as an imageJ plugin with an optional Matlab extension to remove cell bodies. More details are published at <a href=\"http://dev.biologists.org/content/142/12/2213.long\">Kerman et al. 2015 <em>Development</em></a>. Supplemental Material includes a detailed <a href=\"http://dev.biologists.org/content/develop/suppl/2015/06/10/dev.116517.DC1/DEV116517supp.pdf\">user manual</a> and the <a href=\"http://bilalkermanlab.com/cem/\">download link</a>.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-11-16T08:47:48+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-02-07T07:30:01+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1517989967,"last_comment_uid":426,"status":2}],"has_author":[],"has_biological_terms":[{"target_id":4376,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"20014221-044d-4fe5-85a6-b2fec1230060","url":"/taxonomy/term/4376"},{"target_id":4377,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"7be5675f-c61b-48d3-be2b-69348deaa311","url":"/taxonomy/term/4377"}],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"User Manual is included in the compressed file","uri":"http://bilalkermanlab.com/cem/"}],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[],"has_function":[{"target_id":4345},{"target_id":4346},{"target_id":4026,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Neuron_image_analysis","url":"/neuron-image-analysis"},{"target_id":4012,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Dilation","url":"/dilation"},{"target_id":4767,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation___Pixel-based_colocalisation","url":"/pixel-based-colocalisation"},{"t